\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Three invariant channels}
\date{2026-11-21}

\p{On a finite graph, three functions of a gauge configuration
take values in the coefficient ring.}

\p{The \newvocab{vector channel} at a pair of vertices is the
\vocabk{scalar path pairing}{fdip-011B} along a chosen path.}

\p{The \newvocab{orbit-label channel} of a sector is the
function that equals #{1} on configurations of that
\vocabk{sector labeling}{fdip-0121} and #{0} on the others.}

\p{The \newvocab{plaquette channel} of a face is the value of a
\vocabk{class-function kernel}{fdip-012C} on the face word.
The witness edge of \ref{fdip-012P} has no face, and that
channel is absent there. By \ref{fdip-0122}, a site factor
constant on an orbit contributes one constant on that sector.
The link and temporal factors on the edge are that
class-function kernel and the
\vocabk{double-coset kernel}{fdip-012C}.}
